                <pb facs="0427" n="329" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg329"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.05/251: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cunningham</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-01-28T12:00:00+08:00">January 28,
                        1930—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received January 28—1:25 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>The following from Perkins: In view of the Minister’s arrival today I shall be
                    glad to receive soon as possible the Department’s instructions as requested in
                    the Legation’s No. 71 of January 23, 3 p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
